WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.996
These readings ask who decides how powerful technologies are governed.

00:00:04.996 --> 00:00:10.136
They cover gene editing, encryption policy, and artificial intelligence.

00:00:10.136 --> 00:00:13.920
Each asks whether experts alone should set the rules.

00:00:13.920 --> 00:00:19.328
In 1975, scientists met at Asilomar to discuss recombinant DNA.

00:00:19.328 --> 00:00:22.505
Their answer to risk was containment.

00:00:22.505 --> 00:00:28.000
The essay says one thing was missing: a diversity of viewpoints.

00:00:28.000 --> 00:00:31.537
The authors say Asilomar framed risk narrowly.

00:00:31.537 --> 00:00:33.921
Ethics was left off the agenda.

00:00:33.921 --> 00:00:39.151
Copying that model for CRISPR would fail both history and democracy,

00:00:39.151 --> 00:00:41.920
so they urge inclusive deliberation.

00:00:41.920 --> 00:00:45.894
In 1993, the White House announced the Clipper Chip.

00:00:45.894 --> 00:00:49.257
Each device had two keys, stored separately.

00:00:49.257 --> 00:00:53.920
Two independent entities would run the key escrow data banks.

00:00:53.920 --> 00:00:59.131
Agents would need legal authorization, normally a court order, to get keys.

00:00:59.131 --> 00:01:04.481
The algorithm stayed classified, though outside cryptography experts would be

00:01:04.481 --> 00:01:06.080
invited to evaluate it.

00:01:06.080 --> 00:01:12.743
In 2023, an open letter called on all AI labs to pause for at least six months the

00:01:12.743 --> 00:01:16.400
training of systems more powerful than GPT-4.

00:01:16.400 --> 00:01:21.463
The letter says such decisions must not be left to unelected tech leaders.

00:01:21.463 --> 00:01:26.527
If labs will not pause quickly, governments should step in and institute a

00:01:26.527 --> 00:01:27.280
moratorium.

00:01:27.280 --> 00:01:31.395
The lesson is that technology choices are social choices.

00:01:31.395 --> 00:01:36.017
Experts matter, but good governance brings more voices in early,

00:01:36.017 --> 00:01:38.400
before a technology is locked in.
